>technical definition corresponds to my usage. My Random House 
>Unabridged gives: "A single unified awareness derived from sensory 
>processes while a stimulus is present."

Stimuli are distinct from sensations.  Stimuli are outside the nervous
system -- the oncoming photons, sound waves, etc., are stimuli.  Sensations
are caused (in part) by stimuli.

>DK> "Perceptual judgement" is "perception"; there is no "perception"
>DK> independent of the perceiver's evaluation of incoming sense data.
>
>The evaluation by the consciousness is separate from the
>pre-processing of the nervous system.

As I said, this is the central point, and the evidence of neurology
indicates otherwise.
